<div class="section section-z-top "  >
    <div class="bg"></div>
    <section>
      








    <h3 class="heading underlined_title ">Frequently Asked Questions about SIX Swiss Exchange</h3>










    
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/etc.clientlibs/ihcc/components/content/container/accordion/clientlibs.min.ACSHASHc3254a3d67472fe62754ffbd32af0a2e.css" type="text/css">
<script src="/etc.clientlibs/ihcc/components/content/container/accordion/clientlibs.min.ACSHASH0c74b7ab3c4758e8267710172ab51b9c.js"></script>





<div>
    
    
    <div class="accordion" aria-multiselectable="false">
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="trading-time" aria-expanded="false">When does the Swiss stock exchange (SIX Swiss Exchange) open and close on trading days? </button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="trading-time" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>On trading days, the Swiss stock exchange is open from Monday to Friday. Each trading day is divided into five trading periods, the times of which vary depending on the trading segment. Ongoing trading in equities takes place between 9:00 am and 5:30 pm (plus a two-minute random time window for the opening and closing).</p>
<p>Complete information about trading hours can be found <a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/the-swiss-stock-exchange/trading/trading-provisions/trading-hours.html#scrollTo=trading-hours-overview">here</a>.&nbsp;</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="public-holidays" aria-expanded="false">Which public holidays apply to stock exchange trading in Switzerland?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="public-holidays" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>The Swiss stock exchange is closed on federal holidays. All stock exchange holidays are listed in the <a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html">trading calendar</a>.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="ipo" aria-expanded="false">Where can I find information about IPOs on SIX Swiss Exchange?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="ipo" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>Companies inform the public of their intention to go public. A planned initial public offering (IPO) is published on the<a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/shares/ipo-history.html">&nbsp;website&nbsp;of SIX</a> . The lead time varies from company to company. The Swiss Federal Act on Financial Services (FIDLEG) defines the requirements for the listing prospectus that every company must prepare if it wishes to apply for admission of securities to trading on the Swiss stock exchange. The aim is to enable potential investors to make an informed decision about whether to purchase shares in the company. The issuer must publish the prospectus no later than six working days before the end of the bookbuilding period.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="trading-fees" aria-expanded="false">What fees and charges apply when trading via SIX Swiss Exchange?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="trading-fees" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>For professional, officially registered trading participants, the fees and charges for trading on SIX Swiss Exchange vary depending on trading activity. Private investors incur the costs charged by their chosen bank or broker. Here too, there may be differences depending on the trading segment and order types.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="sustainable-investments" aria-expanded="false">What sustainable investment opportunities does SIX offer?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="sustainable-investments" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>SIX enables investments in a wide range of sustainable products, including ETFs, sustainable bonds, structured products, and indices.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/the-swiss-stock-exchange/trading/sustainability.html">Read More</a></p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
            
                





    
    
    
    

    <button class="expander-trigger " aria-controls="smi-spi" aria-expanded="false">What is the difference between the Swiss Market Index (SMI) and the Swiss Performance Index (SPI)?</button>

    
    
    
    




<div data-expander-id="smi-spi" class="expander-body " role="region" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="expander-body-inner">
        



<div  class="textimage ">
    <div class="">
                    <div><p>The <a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/indices/switzerland/equity/smi.html">SMI</a>&nbsp;is the leading blue chip index for the Swiss stock market and one of the world's most respected benchmarks. It comprises the 20 largest and most liquid companies in Switzerland. The <a href="https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/indices/switzerland/equity/spi.html">SPI</a>&nbsp;is Switzerland’s most widely followed broad stock market index. To qualify for the SPI, at least 20% of a stock’s shares must be freely tradable.</p></div></div>
        </div>


    </div>
</div>

            
            
        
    </div>
</div>
</section>
    </div>
